WHAT THIS FIXES

This patch fixes:

- adds runtime JSON Schema validation for outgoing VVReport at Post V&V return boundary
- validates required VVReport fields through active schema
- validates additionalProperties constraints through active schema
- resolves common schema refs locally
- converts outgoing validation failure into safe schema-conforming rejected VVReport
- preserves incoming ResultProposal schema validation
- preserves manual policy/safety checks


WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX

This patch does not fix:

- does not align EvidenceItem.kind
- does not align artifact_type
- does not validate every runtime artifact
- does not modify schemas
- does not modify GT
- does not modify Root
- does not modify DRS writeback
- does not claim production readiness
- does not claim public-auditor readiness
- does not close all findings


OVERCLAIM GUARDRAILS

Do not describe this patch as broad runtime schema validation completion.
Do not say every runtime artifact is schema-validated.
Do not say EvidenceItem.kind is aligned.
Do not say artifact_type is aligned.
Do not say this creates production readiness.
Do not say this creates public-auditor readiness.
Do not say GT, Root, or DRS were changed.

Accurate wording:

- Post V&V incoming ResultProposal and outgoing VVReport boundaries are runtime-schema validated.
- EvidenceItem.kind vocabulary alignment remains open.
- artifact_type vocabulary mapping remains open.
- Root remains final authority.


